## B. AI Speech Analyst

Supports oral storytelling practice.

Where a suitable audio-analysis service is connected, provide feedback on:
- Pronunciation.
- Intonation.
- Speaking pace.
- Fluency.
- Clarity.
- Expression.

Make the difference between actual audio analysis and approximate feedback clear.

## C. AI Improvement Tracker

Allow students to compare their first and second attempts.

Display meaningful improvements in a simple visual progress report.

Focus on learning progress, not merely numerical scores.

## D. Adaptive Learning

Implement adaptive learning throughout the missions.

Examples:
- If a student struggles to identify story elements, provide additional hints.
- If a student repeatedly struggles with sequencing, provide a simpler guided activity.
- If a student performs well, introduce a more challenging activity.
- If a student needs help with script organisation, provide a structured writing guide.
- If a student needs more oral practice, provide additional opportunities to rehearse.

Adaptive learning must support student development without making the game unnecessarily difficult.

The teacher remains responsible for final educational assessment.

